 right not  so long ago yeah and since the  quote-unquote discovery of america this  country has been built from change so  regardless of race religion  socio-economic class  that change around you looks like it's  up to us to adjust we all are in pursuit  of this american dream right roof over  our head clothes on our back food on the  table  and we want our kids to be raised in a  harmonious society  we have to accept what change is i once  heard something i'll leave everybody  with this change is inevitable growth is  optional and it's up to us to grow with  change you don't have to like love but  coexisting that's something we all can  do  yeah blame somebody else for your  problems and that's where the trouble  begins it's not going to be somebody  else's fault great piece yeah thank you  guys appreciate it all right you can  hear more of my conversation with  journalist michelle norris on today's  cbs morning's podcast you'll learn what  led her to create something very  interesting it's called the race card  project it invites people to distill  their thoughts about race their  experiences their observations into a  sentence of just six words in most years  most of the people responding are white  people interestingly enough

